Now, on to the game.

The early wasn't too exciting, although I did have a few close calls
in/around sokoban.  There was an early weapon shop with Cleaver in it
(Thanks RNG!), a potion shop (that I never fully cleaned out), and a
very large general store.  Sokoban had an amulet of reflection (which
is my preferred variant).

Smokey potions were hallucination.  As soon as I had a unihorn and
several of them blessed, I started quaffing.  The 2nd potion netted a
wish (blessed greased fireproof +2 cloak of magic resistance).  It was
then time to head deep into the mines.  While in mines end (the
catacombs ... usless for a non-caster), I was teased for being
encumbered.  In minetown I put on a ring of conflict, sat back and had
some popcorn while the watch went at it (hoping for leather gloves).
I was not dissapointed.

After leaving the mines, it was time to head for the castle, hoping
for a silver dragon to drop scales along the way.  It didn't happen,
but while cleaning out Ludios for protection an Aleax had his shield
of reflection stolen by a nymph ... if I didn't get SDSM, this was
part of my back-up plan for the Nemesis level.

After cleaning out the Castle (the wand was (0:1) and spent on 2b?
charging, a BoH, and a ring of teleport control, with one charge (and
the wrest) kept in reserve) and the VoTD, I teleported to the bottom
of gehennom and started working my way up.  In Orcus Town, I mad a
bunch of statues.  Juiblex went down without much of a fight (I
started on the downstair and he was dead before he had a chance to
teleport away or engulf).  Bealzebub and Asmodeus were paid off for
less than 10gp (total).

Back at the castle, and with a boatload of loot, I reverse genocided
silver dragons.  While farming for silver dragon scales with a /undead
turning, one of them dropped a wand of wishing (0:2).  I also got
careless and wound up fainted, surrouned by dragons, and not on an
Elbereth.  YIKES!

After that bit of excitement, it was time to do the quest.  It wasn't
too difficult (AC:-25ish and over 200hp).  A third wand of wishing
(0:3) was death-dropped in the Nemesis level.  The nemesis kill was
semi-tense.  It took two /death charges to kill Ashikaga Takauji.
Even with an amulet of life saving, you're not safe if he gets a turn
[2].

The ascension run is where things get interesting, but went by in a
blur.  Rodney double-troubled in the tower, and it took about 8 /death
charges to kill them both.  I used three wishes during the ascension
run (2 cursed potions of gain level, magic marker, and jumping boots
on astral).  I did the planes in 154 turns, despite not jumping before
astral and faffing about slightly once I got there (killing some
hostile angels and wishing for the jumping boots).

After completing the quest, I was never in any serious danger.  I also
had a boatload wand wishes and 2 magic lamps available, "just in
case". :p

